Upgrade the control plane node from the current minor version to the next patch/minor version

There are two different types of upgrades:

):Patch upgrade
Example: v1.30.4 → v1.30.5
The patch number changes. This usually contains bug and security fixes.

):Minor upgrade
Example: v1.30.4 → v1.31.0
The minor version changes from 30 to 31. Kubernetes upgrades should proceed one minor version at a time.

):What are we actually upgrading?
The control plane node runs important Kubernetes components.
Component	Purpose
API server	Receives kubectl requests
Scheduler	Decides which node should run a Pod
Controller  manager	Maintains the desired cluster state
etcd	    Stores Kubernetes cluster data
kubelet	    Manages Pods on the node

When you upgrade the control plane using kubeadm, you upgrade Kubernetes components and packages as required by the target version.

The exact process depends on your installation and target version

):For a kubeadm-based cluster, the key packages are:
- kubeadm — performs the cluster upgrade.
- kubelet — manages Pods on the node.
- kubectl — command-line client; its version is managed separately.

